URSS RL EVACUATION ROADMAP

v0.0 — Basic two-exit queue model ✓ DONE
│
├── State: (input, left queue, right queue)
├── Actions: route LEFT / RIGHT
├── Fixed stochastic exit probabilities
├── Reward based on people remaining unevacuated
├── Gymnasium custom environment
├── Tabular Q-learning
└── Baselines:
    ├── Random
    ├── Always left/right
    └── Alternating


v0.1 — Asymmetric exits ✓ DONE
│
├── Different exit probabilities
│   e.g. pLeft = 0.7, pRight = 0.3
├── Added stronger baselines
│   ├── Capacity-weighted random
│   └── Expected-time heuristic
├── Q-learning vs heuristic comparison
└── Investigated learned policy/Q-values
    └── Found state-dependent behaviour based on
        remaining input population


v0.2 — Congestion-dependent throughput ← CURRENT
│
├── Exit probability depends on corridor population
│
│   p(q):
│     0.5   q ≤ 2
│     0.3   3–5
│     0.2   6–9
│     0.1   ≥10
│
├── Congestion can create feedback loops
├── Static expected-time heuristic
├── Dynamic expected-time heuristic
├── Tabular Q-learning
└── Compare learned policy against heuristics


────────────────────────────────────


v0.3 — First spatial/grid environment ← NEXT
│
├── 2D grid representation
├── Walls
├── Floor cells
├── Exit cells
├── Initially ONE pedestrian
├── State initially just pedestrian position:
│       (row, column)
├── Actions:
│       UP / DOWN / LEFT / RIGHT
├── One-cell movement per timestep
├── Invalid movement blocked by walls
├── Reward: initially -1 per timestep
└── Terminate when pedestrian reaches exit

Purpose:
Learn/test the spatial simulation mechanics before
adding crowd behaviour and evacuation guidance.


v0.4 — Multiple pedestrians
│
├── Several pedestrians on grid
├── One pedestrian per cell initially
├── Collision / occupied-cell rules
├── Multiple pedestrian movement each timestep
├── Pedestrian locations become dynamic environment state
└── Evacuation ends when all pedestrians leave


v0.5 — Guidance-based control
│
├── Stop treating RL as directly moving pedestrians
├── Pedestrians become part of environment
├── RL agent becomes evacuation guidance system
├── Guidance decisions at junctions / selected cells
├── Pedestrians follow guidance automatically
└── Compare guidance strategies


v0.6 — Building structure
│
├── Multiple corridors
├── Multiple exits
├── Walls / rooms
├── Junctions
├── Different corridor lengths
├── Bottlenecks
└── Travel time now matters


v0.7 — More realistic scenarios
│
├── Random initial pedestrian distributions
├── Different crowd sizes
├── Different exit capacities
├── Blocked/unavailable exits
├── Random environmental configurations
└── Stronger baseline policies
    ├── Shortest path
    ├── Shortest queue
    ├── Static routing
    └── Capacity-aware routing


